From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: fix H713 TVCAP bus gate bits

The H713 CCU models the two gates in TVCAP bus register 0xd80 at
bits 0 and 1. The vendor kernel's fully symbolized clock descriptors
show bus_hdmi_audio_clk.enable = 0x80000000 and
bus_cap_300M_clk.enable = 0x40000000, both at register 0xd80.
The vendor ccu_gate_enable function loads this enable mask directly
and passes it to ccu_gate_helper_enable.

Stock U-Boot independently writes 0xc0000000 to 0x02001d80.
During HDMI bring-up, requesting bus-cap-300m changed the framework
prepare/enable counts to 1/1 while hardware is_enabled remained false.
Use the actual gate masks so normal clock consumers can enable them.

This corrects the clock definitions only. It does not claim complete
HDMI receiver initialization or fix the wrapper-access lock on its own.

Vendor vmlinux SHA256:
3e0d2d3420e066277021fe78d8398eff3937afdaf00c3625354becfbc398bc04

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h713.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h713.c
@@ -592,9 +592,9 @@
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(vincap_dma_clk, "vincap-dma", "ahb",
 		      0xd74, BIT(31), 0);
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(bus_hdmi_audio_clk, "bus-hdmi-audio", "ahb",
-		      0xd80, BIT(0), 0);
+		      0xd80, BIT(31), 0);
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(bus_cap_300m_clk, "bus-cap-300m", "ahb",
-		      0xd80, BIT(1), 0);
+		      0xd80, BIT(30), 0);
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(hdmi_audio_clk, "hdmi-audio", "ahb",
 		      0xd84, BIT(31), 0);
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE(bus_tvcap_clk, "bus-tvcap", "ahb",
